.TH "CPS-INFO" 1 "" "CPS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\&cps\-info \- \&Describe an installed package, or the newest available version of another
.SH SYNOPSIS
.HP 4
.B \&cps info [OPTIONS] <NAME[@VERSION]>
.SH ARGUMENTS
.PP
.B \&<NAME[@VERSION]>
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \&\-\-root <IMAGE>
\&Image root (default: the running system) [default: /]
.TP
.B \&\-\-available
\&Describe the newest version in the signed catalogs even when the package is installed
.TP
.B \&\-\-manifest
\&Print the whole verified manifest in KDL
.PP
.B \&\-\-json
.TP
.B \&\-h, \-\-help
\&Print help
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B \&0
\&Success. A check found nothing to report.
.TP
.B \&1
\&An error.
.TP
.B \&2
\&Invalid usage, such as an unknown option or a missing argument.
.TP
.B \&3
\&A check found something: updates are available (upgrade \-\-check), verification found problems (verify, publisher audit\-builds), pins are stale (recipe repin \-\-check), configuration or images differ (config diff, image diff), manifest dependencies are missing (manifest dependencies), or nothing matched (search, owner).
.TP
.B \&4
\&A confirmation prompt was declined.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cps (1)
